-- title:
--   Edge points lie on two consecutive chain components
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L71). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O$ from the base ring [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.R q`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L32) (the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt q`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb Q$), whose maximal ideal is assumed to be the principal ideal generated by the image of $q$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$. Assume the site hypotheses $H$ of [`V3AsmLevel.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L270): finiteness of the node set $\mathrm{Node} = \mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,\kappa\,\tau\,0 \times \mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,\kappa\,\tau\,1$ (with $\tau = \mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$), existence of oriented crossing charts, an étale-neighbourhood datum, injectivity and closedness of the associated crossing points $\mathrm{xpt}$, and the model hypotheses for $q$ and $O$; assume also $h_\xi$, that each of the points $\xi_j$ lies in `X0` for the chart input $C$, i.e. in the open complement of the finitely many marked points. Write $Y$ for the glued scheme attached to this data, $e_n$ for its widths (the `thick` function of $C$), $\mathrm{comp}$ for the family of invertible ideal sheaf data indexed by chain positions, and $\mathrm{edgePt}$ for the edge points. The conclusion: for every node $n$ and every $d$ with $0 \le d < e_n$, the point $\mathrm{edgePt}(n,d)$ of $Y$ lies in the intersection of the supports of $\mathrm{comp}(\mathrm{chainPos}(e,n,d))$ and $\mathrm{comp}(\mathrm{chainPos}(e,n,d+1))$, where $\mathrm{chainPos}(e,n,\cdot)$ sends $0$ to the first end component, $0 < d < e_n$ to the interior component indexed by $(n, d-1)$, and $d \ge e_n$ to the second end component.
--
--   This is the incidence statement for the chain of $\mathbb P^1$'s inserted at a node when resolving the Deligne–Rapoport model: each of the $e_n$ edge points of the chain above a crossing $n$ lies on exactly the two components adjacent to it in the chain. It is one of the field verifications used in the construction of a `DRResolvedModelPackageLevel` together with ramified resolved charts, namely in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam).
